DR Congo and Rwanda clashed Saturday over the leadership of the Francophonie, as tensions between the neighbouring countries spilled into the race to head the 53-member organisation. French President Emmanuel Macron urged Rwanda to withdraw its candidate in favour of a compromise choice ahead of Monday's vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1dfdc724-e039-11f1-b629-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36JD2YF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1dfdc724-e039-11f1-b629-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36JD2YF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b57f6e5a-e038-11f1-98ff-014aaf8109a4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:54:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1dfdc724-e039-11f1-b629-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36JD2YF.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'I never imagined my father was a Nazi': Born in a German-run 'baby factory'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-i-never-imagined-my-father-was-a-nazi-born-in-a-german-run-baby-factory</link><description>
Two trainloads of children, some of them born in Nazi-run "Lebensborn" maternity homes, were brought from Germany to Commercy in eastern France in 1946. One of them was Édith Pagot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9490f12c-c0c2-11f1-985b-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/main-lebensborn.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9490f12c-c0c2-11f1-985b-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/main-lebensborn.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2bc3236-de96-11f1-87c1-c361ac36d5a6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:25:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9490f12c-c0c2-11f1-985b-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/main-lebensborn.png">© Studio graphique FMM</source><dc:creator>Stéphanie TROUILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans</link><description>
A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a3a881c-e024-11f1-8dfc-13f9b3b00dd2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:15:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Inside Ethiopia's war: Rare access to a hospital treating victims of renewed fighting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting</link><description>
Ethiopia's renewed conflict is taking an increasing toll on civilians, with humanitarian organisations reporting a rise in casualties. In the Amhara region, FRANCE 24’s correspondent Tom Canetti was granted rare access to a civilian hospital where surgeons are struggling to treat the influx of wounded patients. But for many caught in the fighting, reaching medical care is a challenge in itself.
 
Warning: The report contains images of surgery that may be confronting for some viewers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5f45c22-e022-11f1-9671-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-090947-091144-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5f45c22-e022-11f1-9671-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-090947-091144-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb429b9e-e022-11f1-89f0-03213c6d6be3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:23:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world</link><description>
From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">405d92aa-e01f-11f1-9579-21782230ef7c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>U2 releases first new studio album in a decade, 'Caranaval de Luz'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/u2-releases-first-new-studio-album-in-a-decade-caranaval-de-luz</link><description>
U2 just released a new album after nine years of no new content. And fans are already rocking out to the new songs. Details on the Irish rock band’s comeback by Ophelie Jacobson.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63928f76-e01c-11f1-9567-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-082432-082622-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63928f76-e01c-11f1-9567-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-082432-082622-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68c75a12-e01c-11f1-8e4e-0b9a36cadea9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:17:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81c01db6-e01b-11f1-9964-ef92d80b1580</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:17:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Microsoft's widespread outages caused global chaos, including in the healthcasre industry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/microsoft-s-widespread-outages-caused-global-chaos-including-in-the-healthcasre-industry</link><description>
Microsoft says it is seeing improvements in its service availability after an hours-long disruption knocked out its platforms including Outlook and Teams. The outage has affected hundreds of millions of people across the globe. The healthcare industry was among those impacted, as Ophelie Jacobson explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0281a17e-e01a-11f1-bec4-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080413-080559-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0281a17e-e01a-11f1-bec4-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080413-080559-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b062784-e01a-11f1-ab65-3bb9e1c8e9ed</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:07:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France fend off South African comeback to clinch long-awaited win in Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261114-france-fend-off-south-african-comeback-to-clinch-long-awaited-win-in-paris</link><description>
Twenty-one years after last beating the Springboks in Paris, Les Bleus held out for a 21-19 win over the world champions on Friday after a nailbiting finale. Antoine Dupont and company are now one step away from reaching the Nations Championship final in London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0732732e-dfe8-11f1-801a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-France-celebrate.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0732732e-dfe8-11f1-801a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-France-celebrate.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d4ed694-dfec-11f1-a9d3-c34ef6f62c59</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:58:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership</link><description>
President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0675832e-e013-11f1-8769-fbca886990f0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:30:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg">© Peter Morrison, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump</link><description>
A delegation of 18 Democratic lawmakers arrived at the COP31 climate summit in Turkey on Saturday to reaffirm the US commitment to tackling global warming following their sweeping midterm election victory. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c9485ba-e019-11f1-9673-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/91b19f88637d15a0b0843d352f4b999ad0eb540a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c9485ba-e019-11f1-9673-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/91b19f88637d15a0b0843d352f4b999ad0eb540a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b37f1ff6-e015-11f1-8b19-516280fe1689</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:25:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c9485ba-e019-11f1-9673-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/91b19f88637d15a0b0843d352f4b999ad0eb540a.jpg">© Laurent Thomet, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight</link><description>
Elon Musk’s SpaceX successfully launched its Starship, the world's largest spaceship, into orbit where it should release 15 satellites for its Starlink network. A few minutes after lift off however, the rocket's booster which was meant to return to the pad splashed down in the Gulf of Mexico. Details by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb59b9c4-e013-11f1-9576-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-101129-101300-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb59b9c4-e013-11f1-9576-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-101129-101300-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0affadc-e013-11f1-bbac-c37e651db0a2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:21:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Can Nvidia survive without tech titan Jensen Huang?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/can-nvidia-survive-without-tech-titan-jensen-huang</link><description>
The Financial Times says computing giant Nvidia has approached Rene Haas, CEO of British chip designer Arm, in its search for a potential successor to Jensen Huang. Huang resigned after his affair with an alleged Chinese spy. Meanwhile some employees are clamouring for Huang's return – as his fellow tech leader Elon Musk. A sign of Huang's lingering star power, in an industry where so often the fate of each giant company depends on one man. Story by Peter O'Brien.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289dfed6-e013-11f1-a54f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100838-101020-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289dfed6-e013-11f1-a54f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100838-101020-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2db43124-e013-11f1-8edc-e90bbd10ccfb</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:20:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's school principals say threats and violence have become unbearable</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-school-principals-say-threats-and-violence-have-become-unbearable</link><description>
Headteachers gathered across France this Friday, to demonstrate their frustration after nearly two months of student protests that have blockaded high schools. Many of the teachers support the students, but say they feel exhausted and isolated as the violence has surged. They are calling the government to protect them. Story by Vedika Bahl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d44fe2-e012-11f1-9c3a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100620-100800-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d44fe2-e012-11f1-9c3a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100620-100800-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c5994fe-e012-11f1-915b-8567c7828824</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:17:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France protests for fifth Saturday against living costs and heavy-handed policing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-protests-for-fifth-saturday-against-living-costs-and-heavy-handed-policing</link><description>
Different causes are set to come together for one march in Paris this Saturday. Campaign groups, students and Yellow Vest protesters are due to join forces in the capital, bringing together demands on wages, education and civil liberties. But after weeks of demonstrations, union leaders warn that protest fatigue is setting in, while police officers are seeking better compensation for the risk of policing the protests. Story by Jack Pownall.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d23ba148-e011-11f1-8b8d-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100425-100557-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d23ba148-e011-11f1-8b8d-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100425-100557-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d73a7854-e011-11f1-a834-8b7999d8829a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:15:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data</link><description>
On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8cfa494-e011-11f1-8d16-95a3d2c4d031</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:14:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Live: France deploys 70,000 police for new wave of anti-government protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-live-france-mobilises-in-fifth-wave-of-student-protests</link><description>
Between 50 and 60 marches are expected in France on Saturday, according to Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez, who plans to mobilise approximately 70,000 police officers and gendarmes across the country. In Paris, the march will commence at 2pm from Place de la République heading towards Place de la Nation via Bastille.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a63b34f6-e02e-11f1-8824-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T125840Z-625078051-RC2ONOA3SI00-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a63b34f6-e02e-11f1-8824-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T125840Z-625078051-RC2ONOA3SI00-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eec63c5a-dff9-11f1-bb69-5d10c398bef4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:09:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a63b34f6-e02e-11f1-8824-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T125840Z-625078051-RC2ONOA3SI00-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Benoît Tessier, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Microsoft says all services 'fully recovered' after global outage</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261114-microsoft-says-consumer-products-fully-recovered-business-services-improving</link><description>
The tech giant confirmed on Saturday morning that all services have recovered ⁠across ‌Teams, Outlook, Copilot and ⁠other applications, ​ending a ‌global outage ‌that ​crippled online communications across businesses and ​governments ​for ​over 24 hours. The US homeland security chief confirmed there was 'no Microsoft link' to the US air traffic stoppage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847567e0-dfef-11f1-93ed-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313848301021.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847567e0-dfef-11f1-93ed-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313848301021.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59f26c64-dff1-11f1-afb3-bd550d138e40</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:07:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847567e0-dfef-11f1-93ed-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313848301021.jpg">© Lindsey Wasson, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>China to host first-ever trilateral meeting between Trump, Xi and Putin next week</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says</link><description>
The three leaders are scheduled to meet on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen on Thursday, the White House confirmed. US officials said discussions will include nuclear weapons and the war in Iran, but that the war in Ukraine is unlikely to be on the agenda. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned the talks could prove a Yalta-like "redistribution of spheres of influence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8eea7aea-dfe9-11f1-be77-3f507754147d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:09:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg">© Dmitri Lovetsky, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FAA lifts nationwide ground stop on all US flights</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-on-all-us-flights</link><description>
The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage.
